<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
  <section xml:id="two-d-games-space-farm-04-main-scene">
    <title>Main Scene</title>
    <introduction>
    <p>
        The Main Scene holds a Player and a Timer for planting
        the crystals. The Player spawns in the middle of the 
        screen at the beginning of the game, and a new crystal
        is planted at random time intervals in a random location 
        anywhere on the screen.
    </p>
    </introduction>
    <subsection xml:id="two-d-games-space-farm-main-scene-nodes">
      <title>Adding the Nodes</title>
      <p>
        The root node of the Main scene should be a Node, and then rename
        it to Main. Add an instance of player as a child of Main, then
        add a Timer and rename it PlantTimer. Then you are ready to make the 
        script.
      </p>
      </subsection>
      <subsection xml:id="two-d-games-space-farm-main-scene-script">
      <title>Main Script</title>
      <p>
        The script will randomly plant crystals. To 
        do this, the following member variables are needed.
        A <c>PackedScene</c> called <c>crystal</c> will allow the
        Prize to be instantiated. A <c>Vector2i</c> called view_size
        will allow the player and crystals to spawn inside the visible 
        area. One more member variable for score is added in anticipation
        for when the score will be displayed.
      </p>
      <program language="gdscript">
extends Node

var view_size : Vector2i
var crystal: PackedScene = load("res://prize.tscn")
var score: int = 0
   </program>
    <p>
        The next thing we need is a helper function to
        update the view size.
    </p>
    <program language="gdscript">
func update_view_size() -> void:
    view_size = get_viewport().get_visible_rect().size
    get_viewport().size_changed.connect(update_view_size)
    </program>
    <p>
        The ready function will update the view size
        position the player, and then plant a crystal.
    </p>
    <program language="gdscript">
func _ready() -> void:
    update_view_size()
    $Player.position.x = view_size.x/2
    $Player.position.y = view_size.y/2
    plant_crystal()
    </program>
    <p>
        The plant_crystal() helper method creates a Prize,
        randomly places it on the screen, connects its signals to 
        the appropriate methods, adds the prize as a child,
        and then has the Plant timer start for a random time between
        2 and 5 seconds.
    </p>
    <program language="gdscript">
func plant_crystal() -> void:
    var prize: Prize = crystal.instantiate()
    prize.position = Vector2(randf() * view_size.x,
                        randf() * view_size.y)
    add_child(prize)
    $PlantTimer.start(randf()*3+2)
    </program>
    <p> 
        Next we need to connect the PlantTimer's timeout()
        to the plant_crystal() method.
    </p>
    <p>
        We need to change one more project setting. In the
        Project Settings, Display, Window, Strecth. Set the 
        Mode value to "canvas_items",and then we are finished
        building the main scene.
    </p>
    
      </subsection>
      <subsection xml:id="two-d-games-space-farm-main-scene-play-testing">
      <title>Play Testing</title>
      <p>
        Now, run the main scene, and look at the sizes of
        each of the items on the screen. Change the scale 
        of each to make sure that they are all about the 
        same size when at the maximum size. Or you could 
        make it so that the largest crystal is bigger than
        the ship. The lasso should fit completely around 
        the largest crystal before it disappears.
      </p>
      <p>Once you are finished play testing, go to the next 
        section to make basic interactions for game play to work.
      </p>
      </subsection>
    </section>
